   'rounds_reps',
   'Buriak honors U.S. Navy AWS1 James Buriak, 31, of Salem, Virginia, a naval aircrewman rescue swimmer with HSC-8. He died on Aug. 31, 2021, when his helicopter, Loosefoot 616, went down off the coast of San Diego, California.

You get 20 minutes to complete as many rounds as possible of 5 squat cleans (155 lb / 135 lb), 10 burpees over the bar, 15 pull-ups and a 200 m run. The women''s load is close to the men''s, so the cleans are heavy for everyone. The burpees and pull-ups come straight after, and the short run gives you very little time to recover before the bar again.',
   '[{"name": "Squat Cleans", "reps": "5", "tip": "Catch in a full front squat and stand tall. Quick singles are fine at this load.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "135 lb"}, {"name": "Burpees Over the Bar", "reps": "10", "tip": "Jump or step over the bar after each burpee. Stay close to the bar so you do not waste steps."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "15", "tip": "Chin over the bar on every rep. Break into small sets before your grip fails."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Run at a steady pace and use the way back to plan your next set of cleans."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps.',
   '["Pick a clean load you can move for singles all 20 minutes", "Small sets on the pull-ups save your grip", "Keep moving on the run, even if it is slow"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set a pace in the first round that you can hold for the full 20 minutes.", "On the squat cleans, keep the bar close and drive your elbows through fast so you catch it on your shoulders, not your wrists.", "Treat the burpees over the bar as steady work and breathe at the top of each one.", "Plan your pull-ups in sets, such as 8 and 7 or 5, 5 and 5, and start the next set before you feel ready.", "Count your rounds on a whiteboard or with a counter so your score is accurate."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the squat cleans to 95 lb / 65 lb, or swap in power cleans plus front squats if a full squat catch is not ready yet. Use step-over burpees instead of jumping, and replace pull-ups with jumping pull-ups or ring rows. Cut the pull-ups to 10 per round if your grip limits you early.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Buriak workout?", "answer": "As many rounds and reps as possible in 20 minutes of 5 squat cleans (155 lb / 135 lb), 10 burpees over the bar, 15 pull-ups and a 200 m run."}, {"question": "How is Buriak scored?", "answer": "Your score is total rounds plus any extra reps you complete before the 20 minutes end."}, {"question": "Who was Buriak?", "answer": "AWS1 James Buriak, 31, of Salem, Virginia, a U.S. Navy aircrewman rescue swimmer with HSC-8. He died on Aug. 31, 2021, when his helicopter went down off the coast of San Diego."}, {"question": "What weight is used for the squat cleans?", "answer": "155 lb for men and 135 lb for women. Scale to a load you can clean for steady singles."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=laqGO4zBCvM'),
  ('Cameron',
   'cameron',
