   'time',
   'Cameron honors U.S. Coast Guard Lt. Junior Grade Thomas Cameron, 24, of Portland, Oregon, who was in training at the Aviation Training Center in Mobile, Alabama. He died on Feb. 28, 2012, when his unit''s helicopter crashed into Mobile Bay during a training mission.

This is a long chipper of ten movements done once each, in order. The reps switch between 50 and 25: walking lunge steps, chest-to-bar pull-ups, box jumps (24 in / 20 in), triple-unders, back extensions, ring dips, knees-to-elbows, wall-ball "two-for-ones" (20 lb / 14 lb), sit-ups and finally 5 rope climbs to 15 feet. The triple-unders and rope climbs are the big skill tests, and they come when you are already tired.',
   '[{"name": "Walking Lunges", "reps": "50 steps", "tip": "Each step counts as one rep. Touch the back knee down lightly and keep your chest up."}, {"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "25", "tip": "Your chest must touch the bar. Break into sets of 5 to 8 early."}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "50", "tip": "Step down instead of rebounding to protect your Achilles tendons and save energy.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Triple-Unders", "reps": "25", "tip": "The rope passes under your feet three times per jump. Jump a little higher and spin fast from the wrists."}, {"name": "Back Extensions", "reps": "50", "tip": "Move from the hips on a GHD or back extension bench, and stop at a straight body line."}, {"name": "Ring Dips", "reps": "25", "tip": "Lower until your shoulders are below your elbows, then press to full lockout."}, {"name": "Knees-to-Elbows", "reps": "50", "tip": "Use short sets and a steady swing. Rest before your grip forces you off the bar."}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "25 two-for-ones", "tip": "CrossFit calls these two-for-ones. Many gyms count two wall-ball shots as one rep here, for 50 throws in all.", "rx_men": "20 lb", "rx_women": "14 lb"}, {"name": "Sit-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Touch the floor behind your head and your feet at the top. Use an abmat if you have one."}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "5", "tip": "Use a foot lock to save your arms. Climb to 15 feet and come down under control.", "rx_men": "15 ft", "rx_women": "15 ft"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Pace the first half so you can still climb at the end", "Have a triple-under plan, since misses add up fast", "Save your grip for the rope climbs"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set up every station before you start so you never stop to hunt for gear.", "Break the chest-to-bar pull-ups and knees-to-elbows into small sets from the start, because the rope climbs at the end need your grip.", "If triple-unders are new to you, practice a few before the workout so you know your timing.", "Wall-ball targets are 10 feet for men and 9 feet for women, and the ball must hit the target to count.", "Use a foot lock on every rope climb and lower yourself hand over hand rather than sliding."]'::jsonb,
   'Replace triple-unders with 50 double-unders or 75 single-unders. Use regular pull-ups or jumping pull-ups for chest-to-bar, bench or box dips for ring dips, and hanging knee raises for knees-to-elbows. Step up on the box, use a lighter wall ball, do back extensions on the floor as superman raises, and swap each rope climb for 3 lying rope pulls to standing.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Cameron workout?", "answer": "For time: 50 walking lunge steps, 25 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 50 box jumps (24 in / 20 in), 25 triple-unders, 50 back extensions, 25 ring dips, 50 knees-to-elbows, 25 wall-ball two-for-ones (20 lb / 14 lb), 50 sit-ups and 5 rope climbs to 15 feet."}, {"question": "What is a wall-ball two-for-one?", "answer": "CrossFit uses the term without a full definition. Many gyms count two wall-ball shots as one rep, so the 25 two-for-ones become 50 throws."}, {"question": "Who was Cameron?", "answer": "U.S. Coast Guard Lt. Junior Grade Thomas Cameron, 24, of Portland, Oregon. He died on Feb. 28, 2012, when his unit''s helicopter crashed into Mobile Bay during a training mission."}, {"question": "What equipment do I need for Cameron?", "answer": "A pull-up bar, rings, a box, a jump rope, a GHD or back extension bench, a medicine ball and a climbing rope."}]'::jsonb,
