   'time',
   'Capoot honors Officer James Lowell Capoot, 45, of the Vallejo Police Department in California. He died in the line of duty on Nov. 17, 2011, while chasing an armed man suspected of robbing a bank. He served as a motorcycle officer, motorcycle instructor, driving instructor and SWAT officer.

The push-ups go down while the runs get longer: 100 push-ups, 800 m run, 75 push-ups, 1,200 m run, 50 push-ups, 1,600 m run, 25 push-ups and a 2,000 m run. That is 250 push-ups and 5,600 m of running. The early push-up sets are the hardest on your chest and arms, and the last two runs test your aerobic engine.',
   '[{"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "100", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top. Start with sets you can repeat, such as 10 to 15."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Shake out your arms as you run and settle into a pace you can hold."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "75", "tip": "Keep a straight body line. Rest in the top position, not on the floor."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1,200 m", "tip": "Stay relaxed. Your heart rate will come down as you find your stride."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Shorter sets are fine. Keep the rest between them short."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1,600 m", "tip": "This is where a steady pace pays off."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "25", "tip": "Your arms will be tired, so focus on full range on every rep."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "2,000 m", "tip": "The longest run comes last. Empty the tank in the final 400 m."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Break the first 100 push-ups early", "Run at a pace you can hold for 5,600 m", "Full range on every push-up"]'::jsonb,
   '["Plan your first set of 100 push-ups as many small sets, because going to failure early slows every set after it.", "Lower your chest all the way to the floor and lock your arms at the top, or the rep does not count.", "Squeeze your glutes and brace your core so your hips do not sag as you tire.", "Treat the first run as recovery for your arms, then build your pace on the longer runs.", "Measure your running route before you start so each distance is accurate."]'::jsonb,
   'Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box or bench, and halve the reps to 50, 38, 25 and 13 if needed. Shorten the runs to 400 m, 600 m, 800 m and 1,000 m, or row the same distances if you cannot run.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Capoot workout?", "answer": "For time: 100 push-ups, 800 m run, 75 push-ups, 1,200 m run, 50 push-ups, 1,600 m run, 25 push-ups and 2,000 m run."}, {"question": "How many push-ups and how far do you run in Capoot?", "answer": "250 push-ups and 5,600 m of running in total."}, {"question": "Who was Capoot?", "answer": "Officer James Lowell Capoot, 45, of the Vallejo Police Department. He died in the line of duty on Nov. 17, 2011, while chasing an armed bank robbery suspect."}, {"question": "Do I need any equipment for Capoot?", "answer": "No. You only need space to do push-ups and a route to run."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3AQ-YY2biUA'),
