   'time',
   'Carse honors U.S. Army Cpl. Nathan B. Carse, 32, of Harrod, Ohio, assigned to the 2nd Engineer Battalion, 176th Engineer Brigade, based at White Sands Missile Range, New Mexico. He died in Kandahar, Afghanistan, on Feb. 8, 2011, from wounds suffered when insurgents attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device.

You work down a ladder of 21-18-15-12-9-6-3 reps of squat cleans (135 lb / 95 lb), double-unders, deadlifts (185 lb / 125 lb) and box jumps (24 in / 20 in). Every round starts with a 50 m bear crawl, so you crawl seven times in all. That adds up to 84 reps of each movement and 350 m of bear crawl. The early rounds are long and heavy, and the bear crawls tax your shoulders before every barbell set.',
   '[{"name": "Bear Crawls", "reps": "50 m", "tip": "Start every round with this. Hips low, knees just off the floor, and small, quick steps."}, {"name": "Squat Cleans", "reps": "21-18-15-12-9-6-3", "tip": "Catch in a full front squat. Break the big sets into small ones before your grip goes.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Double-Unders", "reps": "21-18-15-12-9-6-3", "tip": "Stay relaxed and spin from your wrists. The sets are short, so aim for no misses."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "21-18-15-12-9-6-3", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs. Use a second bar if you can, so you do not change plates.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "21-18-15-12-9-6-3", "tip": "Step down to save your legs for the cleans in the next round.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Two barbells save you from changing plates", "Break the round of 21 cleans early", "Keep the bear crawl steady, not fast"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set up one bar for squat cleans and a second for deadlifts so you move straight from station to station.", "In the rounds of 21 and 18, plan your clean sets before you start, such as sets of 5 or 7.", "On the bear crawl, keep your back flat and your hips level with your shoulders.", "Hinge from your hips on the deadlifts and keep your lower back neutral, even when you rush.", "The rounds get much shorter after 12, so hold back a little early and push the last three rounds."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the squat cleans to 95 lb / 65 lb and the deadlifts to 135 lb / 95 lb, or use power cleans if a full squat catch is not ready. Replace double-unders with twice as many single-unders, step up on the box, and shorten the bear crawl to 25 m. Starting the ladder at 15 cuts the workout down a lot.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Carse workout?", "answer": "21-18-15-12-9-6-3 reps for time of squat cleans (135 lb / 95 lb), double-unders, deadlifts (185 lb / 125 lb) and box jumps (24 in / 20 in), with a 50 m bear crawl at the start of each round."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Carse?", "answer": "84 reps of each movement, 336 in all, plus seven 50 m bear crawls for 350 m."}, {"question": "Who was Carse?", "answer": "U.S. Army Cpl. Nathan B. Carse, 32, of Harrod, Ohio. He died in Kandahar, Afghanistan, on Feb. 8, 2011, after an improvised explosive device attack on his unit."}, {"question": "Do I bear crawl before every round?", "answer": "Yes. Each of the seven rounds starts with a 50 m bear crawl."}]'::jsonb,
