   'City 100 honors Police Chief Inspector Rouven Laur, 29, of the Baden-Württemberg police force in Mannheim, Germany. He died on May 31, 2024, from knife wounds he suffered on duty while helping a person who had been attacked.

This is a partner workout with a barbell for each partner (155 lb / 105 lb). The team first completes 31 shuttle runs of 7 m down and 7 m back. Then you complete 10 rounds of 7 deadlifts, 7 hang power cleans and a 7 m overhead walking lunge. While one partner works through a round, the other holds a barbell in the front rack, and you switch stations after each round. The front-rack hold means nobody really rests.',
   '[{"name": "Shuttle Run", "reps": "31 trips", "tip": "Each trip is 7 m down and 7 m back. Touch the line at each end."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "7", "tip": "Flat back and the bar close to your legs. This is the start of each round.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Hang Power Cleans", "reps": "7", "tip": "Start from above the knee, drive with your hips and catch with high elbows.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Overhead Walking Lunges", "reps": "7 m", "tip": "Lock the bar overhead with your biceps by your ears. Short, controlled steps.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Front Rack Hold", "reps": "While partner works", "tip": "Hold the bar on your shoulders with high elbows until your partner finishes the round.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your team''s finish time.',
   '["Agree on how to split the shuttle runs before you start", "Keep your elbows high in the front-rack hold", "Switch stations quickly after each round"]'::jsonb,
   '["Agree before the clock starts how you will share the 31 shuttle runs, since CrossFit does not set a split.", "Turn quickly at each line on the shuttle runs and stay low through the turn.", "Move from the deadlifts into the hang power cleans without dropping the bar if you can, then press or jerk it overhead for the lunge.", "In the front-rack hold, rest the bar on your shoulders, not your hands, and breathe steadily.", "Keep the switches tight. A few seconds lost on each of 10 switches adds up."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower both barbells to 95 lb / 65 lb, or use a lighter bar for the hold than for the work. Replace the overhead walking lunge with a front-rack walking lunge if your shoulders are not ready, and cut to 6 rounds if the full 10 would take more than about 35 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the City 100 workout?", "answer": "For time with a partner: 31 shuttle runs (7 m down, 7 m back), then 10 rounds of 7 deadlifts, 7 hang power cleans and a 7 m overhead walking lunge (155 lb / 105 lb). One partner holds a barbell in the front rack while the other completes a round, then you switch."}, {"question": "How are the shuttle runs split?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Most teams split them as evenly as they can or alternate trips."}, {"question": "Who was City 100 named for?", "answer": "Police Chief Inspector Rouven Laur, 29, of the Baden-Württemberg police force in Mannheim, Germany. He died on May 31, 2024, from knife wounds suffered on duty while helping a person who had been attacked."}, {"question": "How do I score City 100?", "answer": "Record the time your team finishes the last round."}]'::jsonb,
