   'time',
   'Clovis honors U.S. Army 2nd Lt. Clovis T. Ray, 34, of San Antonio, Texas, assigned to the 2nd Battalion, 35th Infantry Regiment, 3rd Brigade Combat Team, 25th Infantry Division, based at Schofield Barracks, Hawaii. He was killed on March 15, 2012, in Kunar Province, Afghanistan, when insurgents attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device.

You run 10 miles and complete 150 burpee pull-ups, split up however you like. Some athletes run a mile and then do 15 burpee pull-ups, ten times over. Others do the run in bigger pieces. Either way, this is one of the longest Hero workouts, and the challenge is keeping a steady pace for hours.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "10 miles", "tip": "Split the run into pieces that suit you, such as 1 mile at a time. Start slower than you think you need to."}, {"name": "Burpee Pull-Ups", "reps": "150", "tip": "Do a burpee, then jump to the bar for one pull-up. Chin over the bar on every rep."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Plan your split before you start", "Bring water and fuel for a long effort", "Steady burpee pull-ups beat fast ones"]'::jsonb,
   '["A simple split is 1 mile of running followed by 15 burpee pull-ups, repeated 10 times.", "Keep the run at an easy, conversational pace for the first half.", "Set the bar a little above your reach so you can jump straight into the pull-up from the burpee.", "Drink water and eat small amounts during the workout if it will take you more than about 90 minutes.", "Protect your hands with grips or tape, since 150 pull-ups after long runs can tear skin."]'::jsonb,
   'Cut the run to 5 miles and the burpee pull-ups to 75, keeping the same split. Replace pull-ups with jumping pull-ups or ring rows after the burpee, or use plain burpees. Rowing or biking can replace part of the running if your joints need a break.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Clovis workout?", "answer": "For time: run 10 miles and complete 150 burpee pull-ups. Split the run and burpee pull-ups however you like."}, {"question": "How long does Clovis take?", "answer": "Most athletes need around 1:45 to 3 hours, depending on run pace and how quickly they move through the burpee pull-ups."}, {"question": "Who was Clovis?", "answer": "U.S. Army 2nd Lt. Clovis T. Ray, 34, of San Antonio, Texas, of the 25th Infantry Division. He was killed on March 15, 2012, in Kunar Province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "Do I have to finish the run before the burpee pull-ups?", "answer": "No. CrossFit lets you split the run and the burpee pull-ups however you like."}]'::jsonb,
