   'time',
   'Coffland honors U.S. Army Spc. Christopher J. Coffland, 43, of Baltimore, Maryland, assigned to the 323rd Military Intelligence Battalion at Fort Meade, Maryland. He died on Nov. 13, 2009, in Wardak Province, Afghanistan, of wounds suffered when enemy forces attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device. He was a CrossFit athlete who loved long workouts, heavy lifts and push-ups.

Your goal is to hang from a pull-up bar for a total of 6 minutes. Each time you drop off the bar, you must run 800 m and do 30 push-ups before you get back on. The hang tests your grip, and every drop costs you a long penalty, so staying on the bar as long as possible is the whole game.',
   '[{"name": "Bar Hang", "reps": "6 min total", "tip": "Hang with straight arms and a full grip. Only the time on the bar counts toward 6 minutes."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Penalty for each drop from the bar. Use it to shake out your hands."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "30", "tip": "Also part of each penalty. Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your total time to finish 6 minutes on the bar, including every run and push-up penalty.',
   '["Every drop costs an 800 m run and 30 push-ups", "Chalk up and use a full grip", "Shake out your hands on the run"]'::jsonb,
   '["Use a stopwatch you can pause, or a partner, to track how long you have been on the bar.", "Wrap your thumbs around the bar and keep your shoulders active so the hang stays in your hands, not your joints.", "Shift your grip slightly or let one hand relax for a moment if you can do it without dropping.", "On each penalty, run at a steady pace and keep the push-ups in a few sets so you return to the bar ready.", "Chalk before every return to the bar."]'::jsonb,
   'Cut the total hang to 3 or 4 minutes, or the penalty to a 400 m run and 15 push-ups. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands raised on a box. If you cannot hang for long at all, stand on a box and let it take part of your weight.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Coffland workout?", "answer": "Hang from a pull-up bar for 6 minutes in total. Each time you drop from the bar, run 800 m and do 30 push-ups before you get back on."}, {"question": "How is Coffland scored?", "answer": "Record your total time, from the start until you finish 6 minutes on the bar, including all penalty runs and push-ups."}, {"question": "Who was Coffland?", "answer": "U.S. Army Spc. Christopher J. Coffland, 43, of Baltimore, Maryland, of the 323rd Military Intelligence Battalion. He died on Nov. 13, 2009, in Wardak Province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "Does time on the run count toward the 6 minutes?", "answer": "No. Only time spent hanging from the bar counts."}]'::jsonb,
