   'Cut each movement to 20 reps, or do just one round. Use knee push-ups, a lighter barbell such as 95 lb / 65 lb for deadlifts and 65 lb / 45 lb for clean and jerks, a 20 in box or step-ups, and a lighter ball. Replace pull-ups with jumping pull-ups or ring rows.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Crain workout?", "answer": "2 rounds for time of 34 push-ups, 34 deadlifts (135 lb / 95 lb), 34 box jumps (24 in), 34 clean and jerks (95 lb / 65 lb), 34 burpees, 34 wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb) and 34 pull-ups, with a 50-yard sprint after every movement."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Crain?", "answer": "476 reps in all, 68 of each movement, plus 14 sprints of 50 yards."}, {"question": "Who was Crain?", "answer": "Officer Michael \"Freight\" Crain, 34, of the Riverside Police Department and a former U.S. Marine Corps sergeant. He was fatally shot in an apparent ambush while on patrol on Feb. 7, 2013."}, {"question": "Is the box height the same for women?", "answer": "Yes. CrossFit lists a 24 in box for both men and women in Crain."}]'::jsonb,
