   'time',
   'Dae Han honors U.S. Army Sgt. First Class Dae Han Park, 36, of Watertown, Connecticut, assigned to the 3rd Battalion, 1st Special Forces Group (Airborne), based at Joint Base Lewis-McChord, Washington. He died on March 12, 2011, in Wardak Province, Afghanistan, from wounds suffered when enemy forces attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device.

You complete three rounds of an 800 m run carrying an empty barbell, 3 rope climbs to 15 feet and 12 thrusters (135 lb / 95 lb). Carrying the bar for 800 m wears out your shoulders, arms and grip before you even reach the rope. The heavy thrusters then hit your legs and lungs at the end of each round.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Carry an empty barbell. Switch between holding it in front of you, on your back and at your side."}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "3", "tip": "Use a foot lock to save your arms after the barbell run.", "rx_men": "15 ft", "rx_women": "15 ft"}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "12", "tip": "Drive from the bottom of the squat to press the bar overhead in one motion. Break into small sets.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Change how you carry the bar during the run", "Foot lock on every rope climb", "Break the thrusters before you fail"]'::jsonb,
   '["Load the thruster bar before you start so you only need to grab it after the climbs.", "On the run, carry the bar across your back, in front of your chest or at your side, and switch positions before your grip gives out.", "Lock your feet on the rope and stand up to climb, so your legs do most of the work.", "On the thrusters, keep your elbows high in the squat and let your legs drive the bar up.", "Break the 12 thrusters into sets such as 6 and 6 or 4, 4 and 4 from the first round."]'::jsonb,
   'Run with a PVC pipe or a training bar instead of a full barbell. Lower the thrusters to 95 lb / 65 lb or use dumbbells. Replace each rope climb with 3 lying rope pulls to standing, or climb part of the way up.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Dae Han workout?", "answer": "3 rounds for time of an 800 m run with an empty barbell, 3 rope climbs to 15 feet and 12 thrusters (135 lb / 95 lb)."}, {"question": "Do I really run with a barbell?", "answer": "Yes. You carry an empty barbell for each 800 m run."}, {"question": "Who was Dae Han?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. First Class Dae Han Park, 36, of Watertown, Connecticut, of the 1st Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on March 12, 2011, in Wardak Province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Dae Han?", "answer": "2,400 m of running with the bar, 9 rope climbs and 36 thrusters."}]'::jsonb,
