   'total_reps',
   'Dallas 5 honors the five police officers killed in a sniper ambush in Dallas, Texas, on July 7, 2016: Dallas Police Officer Patricio "Patrick" Zamarripa, Senior Corporal Lorne Ahrens, Officer Michael Krol and Sergeant Michael Smith, and Dallas Area Rapid Transit Officer Brent Thompson.

There are five stations of 5 minutes each, with 1 minute of rest between them. You do as many reps as possible of burpees, then rounds of 7 deadlifts (155 lb / 105 lb) and 7 box jumps (24 in / 20 in), then Turkish get-ups with a dumbbell (40 lb / 30 lb), then rounds of 7 snatches (75 lb / 55 lb) and 7 push-ups, then calories on the rower. Each station hits something different, so pacing each one well is the key.',
   '[{"name": "Burpees", "reps": "5 min max reps", "tip": "Station 1. Find a rhythm you can hold for the full 5 minutes."}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "1 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Get to the deadlift bar and box."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "7 per round", "tip": "Station 2, paired with box jumps. Flat back and the bar close to your legs.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "7 per round", "tip": "Step down to save your legs.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "1 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Grab your dumbbell for the get-ups."}, {"name": "Turkish Get-Ups", "reps": "5 min max reps", "tip": "Station 3. Keep your eyes on the dumbbell and your arm locked. Switch arms as you like.", "rx_men": "40 lb", "rx_women": "30 lb"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "1 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Move to the snatch bar."}, {"name": "Snatches", "reps": "7 per round", "tip": "Station 4, paired with push-ups. Power or squat snatch, with a full lockout overhead.", "rx_men": "75 lb", "rx_women": "55 lb"}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "7 per round", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top."}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "1 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Strap into the rower."}, {"name": "Row for Calories", "reps": "5 min max calories", "tip": "Station 5. Push hard with your legs and keep a steady stroke rate."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total reps from all five stations. Each calorie on the rower counts as one rep.',
   '["Pace each station for the full 5 minutes", "Set up all the equipment before you start", "Use the rest minute to get to the next station"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set up every station in a row so you can move straight to the next one during each rest minute.", "Keep the burpees steady in station 1, because four more stations follow.", "On the Turkish get-ups, keep your arm locked and your eyes on the dumbbell through every step of the movement.", "On the snatches, keep the bar close to your body and catch it with your arms fully locked.", "Write down your reps after each station so your total is accurate."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 95 lb / 65 lb and the snatch to 45 lb / 35 lb, or use dumbbell snatches. Step up on a 20 in box, use a lighter dumbbell or a kettlebell for the get-ups, and do push-ups from your knees. If a full Turkish get-up is new to you, do get-ups to the elbow or hand.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Dallas 5 workout?", "answer": "Five 5-minute stations with 1 minute of rest between them: max burpees; rounds of 7 deadlifts (155 lb / 105 lb) and 7 box jumps (24 in / 20 in); max Turkish get-ups (40 lb / 30 lb dumbbell); rounds of 7 snatches (75 lb / 55 lb) and 7 push-ups; max calories on the rower."}, {"question": "How is Dallas 5 scored?", "answer": "Your score is total reps from all five stations, with each rowing calorie counted as one rep."}, {"question": "Who does Dallas 5 honor?", "answer": "The five officers killed in the Dallas ambush on July 7, 2016: Patrick Zamarripa, Lorne Ahrens, Michael Krol, Michael Smith and Brent Thompson."}, {"question": "How long does Dallas 5 take?", "answer": "29 minutes: five 5-minute stations with four 1-minute rests."}]'::jsonb,
