   'Daniel Ray honors U.S. Air Force Senior Airman Daniel R. Sanchez, 23, of El Paso, Texas, a combat controller with the 23rd Special Tactics Squadron. He was killed in action on Sept. 16, 2010, near Kajran District, Afghanistan, and received the Bronze Star Medal with Valor.

You complete five rounds with a pair of kettlebells (53 lb / 35 lb each): a 25-foot front-rack lunge, 9 strict pull-ups, a 50-foot overhead carry, 16 hand-release push-ups, a 75-foot front-rack carry, 23 air squats, a 100-foot farmers carry and a 400 m run. CrossFit adds that you should wear a weight vest or body armor if you have one. The carries keep your grip, shoulders and core under load the whole time.',
   '[{"name": "Kettlebell Front-Rack Walking Lunges", "reps": "25 ft", "tip": "Hold both kettlebells in the front rack, elbows in. Touch the back knee down lightly.", "rx_men": "2 x 53 lb", "rx_women": "2 x 35 lb"}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "9", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull your chin over the bar."}, {"name": "Kettlebell Overhead Carry", "reps": "50 ft", "tip": "Lock both arms overhead with your biceps by your ears. Ribs down, short steps.", "rx_men": "2 x 53 lb", "rx_women": "2 x 35 lb"}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "16", "tip": "Lift your hands off the floor at the bottom of each rep, then press up as one unit."}, {"name": "Kettlebell Front-Rack Carry", "reps": "75 ft", "tip": "Bells high on your chest, elbows tucked, and steady breathing.", "rx_men": "2 x 53 lb", "rx_women": "2 x 35 lb"}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "23", "tip": "Hips below the knees and stand all the way up."}, {"name": "Farmers Carry", "reps": "100 ft", "tip": "A kettlebell in each hand at your sides. Stand tall and squeeze the handles.", "rx_men": "2 x 53 lb", "rx_women": "2 x 35 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Settle your breathing and shake out your grip before the next round."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Wear a weight vest or body armor if you have one", "Protect your grip for the strict pull-ups", "Set the bells down only when you must"]'::jsonb,
   '["Mark out 25, 50, 75 and 100 feet before you start so every carry is the right distance.", "In the front rack, keep the bells resting on your forearms and chest, not hanging from your hands.", "On the overhead carry, press the bells up with locked elbows and stop to reset if they drift forward.", "Strict pull-ups come right after the lunge, so shake out your hands and start from a full dead hang.", "If you wear a vest, pick a pace for the run that you can hold for all five rounds."]'::jsonb,
   'Use lighter kettlebells, such as 35 lb / 26 lb, or a single kettlebell for each carry. Replace strict pull-ups with banded pull-ups or ring rows, and do the push-ups from your knees. Skip the vest, or cut to 3 rounds if five would take more than about 55 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Daniel Ray workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time with two kettlebells (53 lb / 35 lb): 25 ft front-rack lunge, 9 strict pull-ups, 50 ft overhead carry, 16 hand-release push-ups, 75 ft front-rack carry, 23 air squats, 100 ft farmers carry and a 400 m run."}, {"question": "Do I need a weight vest for Daniel Ray?", "answer": "CrossFit says to wear a weight vest or body armor if you have one. It is optional."}, {"question": "Who was Daniel Ray?", "answer": "U.S. Air Force Senior Airman Daniel R. Sanchez, 23, of El Paso, Texas, a combat controller with the 23rd Special Tactics Squadron. He was killed in action on Sept. 16, 2010, near Kajran District, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Daniel Ray?", "answer": "45 strict pull-ups, 80 hand-release push-ups and 115 air squats, plus 1,250 ft of kettlebell lunges and carries and 2,000 m of running."}]'::jsonb,
