   'time',
   'Desforges honors U.S. Marine Corps Sgt. Joshua Desforges, 23, of Ludlow, Massachusetts, assigned to the 1st Battalion, 6th Marine Regiment, 2nd Marine Division, II Marine Expeditionary Force, based at Camp Lejeune, North Carolina. He was killed on May 12, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan.

You complete five rounds of 12 deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb), 20 pull-ups, 12 clean and jerks (135 lb / 95 lb) and 20 knees-to-elbows. That adds up to 60 heavy deadlifts, 60 clean and jerks and 200 reps on the pull-up bar. Every movement works your grip, so your hands often give out before your lungs do.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "12", "tip": "Flat back and the bar close to your legs. Break into two or three sets before your grip goes.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "20", "tip": "Chin over the bar. Use small sets, such as 5 or 7, to save your grip."}, {"name": "Clean and Jerks", "reps": "12", "tip": "Fast singles are often quicker than tired touch-and-go reps at this load.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Knees-to-Elbows", "reps": "20", "tip": "Short sets and a steady swing. Knees must touch your elbows."}]'::jsonb,
